u | 21.4.0 | DEPLOYED |\n\n| | orachk | 21.4.0 | DEPLOYED |\n\n| | param | 21.4.0 | DEPLOYED |\n\n| | ps | 21.4.0 | DEPLOYED |\n\n| | pstack | 21.4.0 | DEPLOYED |\n\n| | summary | 21.4.0 | DEPLOYED |\n\n| | tail | 21.4.0 | DEPLOYED |\n\n| | triage | 21.4.0 | DEPLOYED |\n\n| | vi | 21.4.0 | DEPLOYED |\n\n+----------------------+--------------+--------------+-------------+\n\n| Development Tools | oratop | 14.1.2 | DEPLOYED |\n\n+----------------------+--------------+--------------+-------------+\n\n| Support Tools Bundle | darda | 2.10.0.R6036 | DEPLOYED |\n\n| | oswbb | 8.3.2 | RUNNING |\n\n| | prw | 12.1.13.11.4 | NOT RUNNING |\n\n\'----------------------+--------------+--------------+-------------\'\n\nNote :-\n\nDEPLOYED : Installed and Available - To be configured or run interactively.\n\nNOT RUNNING : Configured and Available - Currently turned off interactively.\n\nRUNNING : Configured and Available.\n\n### 使用方式\n\n#### 启停方式\n\nTFA运行在Linux和Unix平台上的init，所以，这将是在服务器启动时自动启动。\n\n默认的情况我们把这个脚本命名为init.tfa;\n\n所在位置取决于不同平台，如：\n\n* Linux and Solaris: /etc/init.d/init.tfa\n* Aix: /etc/init.tfa\n* HP-UX: /sbin/init.d/init.tfa\n\n以下命令式在Linux平台下作为例子：\n\n-- 启动\n\n[root@demo1 bin]# tfactl start\n\n-- 停止\n\nroot@demo1 bin]# tfactl stop\n\n-- 重启：\n\n# /etc/init.d/init.tfa restart\n\n#### 收集方式\n\n我们通过调用tfactl的命令和诊断动词diagnostic来控制TFA收集我们期望的诊断信息。Tfactl 提供给用户多种可选择的模式进行收集，如：集一个时间段内的日志信息来减少我们收集日志的量；\n\n具体操作的命令您可以通过以下方式看到：\n\n# $TFA_HOME/bin/tfactl <command> [options]\n\nUsage: /u01/app/tfa/tfa_home/bin/tfactl diagcollect [-all | -database | -asm | -crs | -os | -install | -node | -tag ]\n\n[-since <n><h|d>| -from <time> -to <time> | -for <time>]\n\n[-copy | -nocopy] [-symlink][-notrim]\n\n在下面的例子中，我们使用了 -all，并告诉TFA收集诊断所有类型的日志，从午夜3月13日至3月13日15:00 进行收集。该命令将启动指定的诊断在后台收集所有群集节点上，压缩成zip文件放置在每个节点的TFA_HOME中:\n\n# tfactl diagcollect -all -from "Mar/13/2015" -to "Mar/13/2015 15:00:00"\n\nCollecting data for all components using above parameters...\n\nCollecting data for all nodes\n\nScanning files from Mar/13/2015 00:00:00 to Mar/13/2015 15:00:00\n\nCollection Id : 20150313221957localhost\n\nRepository Location in localhost : /opt/oracle/tfa/tfa_home/repository/\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:02 CST : Collection Name : tfa_Fri_Mar_13_22_19_57_CST_2015.zip\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:02 CST : Scanning of files for Collection in progress...\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:02 CST : Collecting extra files...\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:07 CST : Getting list of files satisfying time range [03/13/2015 00:00:00 CST, 03/13/2015 15:00:00 CST]\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:07 CST : Starting Thread to identify stored files to collect\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:07 CST : Getting List of Files to Collect\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:07 CST : Trimming file : localhost/var/log/messages with original file size : 1.2MB\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:07 CST : Finshed Getting List of Files to Collect\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:08 CST : Collecting ADR incident files...\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:08 CST : Waiting for collection of extra files\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:30 CST : Completed collection of extra files...\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:33 CST : Completed Zipping of all files\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:33 CST : Cleaning up temporary files\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:33 CST : Finished Cleaning up temporary files\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:33 CST : Finalizing the Collection Zip File\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:33 CST : Finished Finalizing the Collection Zip File\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:33 CST : Total Number of Files checked : 222\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:33 CST : Total Size of all Files Checked : 7.4MB\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:33 CST : Number of files containing required range : 4\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:33 CST : Total Size of Files containing required range : 1.6MB\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:33 CST : Number of files trimmed : 1\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:33 CST : Total Size of data prior to zip : 535kB\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:33 CST : Saved 1.2MB by trimming files\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:33 CST : Zip file size : 45kB\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:33 CST : Total time taken : 31s\n\n2015/03/13 22:20:33 CST : Completed collection of zip files.\n\nLogs are being collected to:\n\n/opt/oracle/tfa/tfa_home/repository/collection_Fri_Mar_13_22_19_57_CST_2015_node_all/localhost.tfa_Fri_Mar_13_22_19_57_CST_2015.zip\n\n无论我们用哪种方法对诊断信息进行收集，日志信息都会被打包好放置在$TFA_HOME/repository的目录下，以便您上传该文件给Oracle support工程师。\n\n# 日常运维-常见处理\n\n## 归档问题\n\n【故障现象】\n\n数据库归档使用率超过阈值（阈值可根据客户自己环境进行动态调整）\n\n【处理方案】\n\n1. 登陆故障服务器，快速检查归档空间使用率\n2. 检查归档空间使用率\n\n归档空间使用率高主要有两种情况：\n\n1. FLASHBACK LOG（FLASHBACK日志）使用率高；\n\n通过grid登陆故障服务器，检查FRADG磁盘组使用率及剩余空间\n\n若FRADG Free_MB空间足够，则使用oracle用户以sysdba用户登陆数据库扩容\n\n执行以下命令进行扩容\n\nSQL> alter system set db_recovery_file_dest_size=100g;\n\n【注意】\n\n1. FRADG为FLASHBACK LOG存放的磁盘组（需根据不同环境进行客户化）\n2. 此案例中以扩容100g举例（需根据不同环境进行客户化）\n3. ARCHIVED LOG（归档日志）使用率高。\n\n清理归档日志文件\n\nRMAN> run {\n\nallocate channel c1 type disk;\n\nallocate channel c2 type disk;\n\ndelete noprompt archivelog all completed before \'sysdate-1\';\n\nrelease channel c1;\n\nrelease channel c2;\n\n}\n\n## UNDO问题\n\n【故障现象】\n\n对一张大表进行长事务DML操作时进程异常中断后需读取UNDO进行回滚，伴随有latch:undo 或db file sequential read相关等待系统资源消耗上升，该表相关业务无法正常执行。\n\n【可能故障原因】\n\n长事务操作写入UNDO,当需要回滚时数据量大且对操作资源消耗非常高。\n\n【应急措施】\n\n查回滚事务：\n\nSQL> set lines 160 pages 999\n\nSQL> alter session set nls_date_format=\'yyyy-mm-dd hh24:mi:ss\';\n\nSQL> select a.usn,\n\na.slt,\n\na.seq,\n\na.state,\n\na.undoblockstotal "total",\n\na.undoblocksdone "done",\n\na.undoblockstotal - a.undoblocksdone "todo",\n\ndecode(cputime,\n\n0,\n\n\'unknown\',\n\nsysdate + (((a.undoblockstotal - a.undoblocksdone) /\n\n(a.undoblocksdone / a.cputime)) / 86400)) "estimated time to complete"\n\nfrom v$fast_start_transactions a;\n\n有时候可能查不到，使用下面的脚本，主要关注ktuxesiz有没有在变化\n\nSQL> select addr, ktuxeusn, ktuxeslt, ktuxesqn, ktuxesiz, ktuxesta\n\nfrom x$ktuxe\n\nwhere ktuxecfl like \'%dead%\'\n\nand ktuxesta != \'inactive\';\n\n1. 如果应用许可，建立同结构空表，然后换名后再回插数据;(如果访问频繁无法rename时kill访问的会话再执行rename，允许的话，停监听临时操作)\n2. 如果不能使用空表，则需等待回滚完成，可设置参数开启并发回滚加快回滚速度;\n\n启用并行：\n\nCPU资源较空闲时可:\n\nSQL> alter system set fast_start_parallel_rollback=high;\n\n注：low是2倍cpu数，high是4倍CPU数 ，当并发子进程之间需要的资源冲突时(Wait for a undo 相关等待)，并发的回滚速度不如串行的回滚速度，可fast_start_parallel_rollback 改成 false。这个参数可在线修改，因此改完后再执行查回滚事务的脚本，看速度有没有增加，以选择最适合的模式。需要注意的是，除非cancel/kill的session是parallel DML，否则不会采用并行回滚。\n\n参考文档解释：\n\nFAST_START_PARALLEL_ROLLBACK specifies the degree of parallelism used when recovering terminated transactions. Terminated transactions are transactions that are active before a system failure. If a system fails when there are uncommitted parallel DML or DDL transactions, then you can speed up transaction recovery during startup by using this parameter.\n\n加快速度：\n\nSQL> alter system set "_cleanup_rollback_entries"=400 scope=spfile;\n\n该参数含义:\n\nThe number of undo records processed at one time when rolling back a transaction. Prevents long transactions from freezing out shorter transactions that also need to be rolled back.\n\nThis means that PMON cleans up 20 blocks every 3 minutes.\n\nThe number 20 is the default value of the parameter CLEANUP_ROLLBACK_ENTRIES.\n\nSo PMON is making progress, but it is slow because every 3 minutes PMON wakes up, does 20 blocks and sleeps again.\n\nHOW TO SPEED UP THE CLEANUP OPERATION\n\n-------------------------------------\n\nTo speed up cleanup of killed sessions you can increase the value of the\n\nCLEANUP_ROLLBACK_ENTRIES init.ora parameter. Its value is 20 by default.\n\n## 内存4031问题\n\n4031 问题作为Oracle 数据库的典型问题，需要的搜集信息如下：\n\n* ASH 数据(Active Session History ) Reports. 参考日常运维-工具介绍章节ASH\n* AWR Reports. 参考日常运维-工具介绍章节AWR.\n\n需要根据问题时间长短选择不同时间频度的AWR报告\n\n* 收集OS 性能数据. 参考日常运维-工具介绍章节OSWatcher.\n* 收集heapdump和library cache dump.（对诊断最直接，但会消耗一定的资源）\n* 发生问题时的数据库alert log和生成的trace文件\n\n除此之外，还需要使用一些脚本搜集一些有用信息。\n\n建议从ORA-4031 Common Analysis/Diagnostic Scripts (Doc ID 430473.1) 下载脚本，并且将发生问题时的脚本输出, 并且交给Oracle 进行分析.\n\n脚本收集样例如下：\n\nREM This script is useful to Oracle Support as it focuses on the principle\n\nREM parameters associated with the configuration of the SGA\n\nSetting MBytes\n\n------------------------------------------------------ -----------\n\n16K Cache: 0 0\n\n2K Cache: 0 0\n\n32K Cache: 0 0\n\n4K Cache: 0 0\n\n8K Cache: 0 0\n\nBuffer Cache: 0 0 << ideal to set minimum\n\nJava Pool Size: 0 0\n\nKeep Cache: 0 0\n\nLarge Pool Size: 0 0\n\nLog Buffer: 7024640 7\n\nRecycle Cache: 0 0\n\nSGA Max: 734003200 700\n\nSGA Target: 612368384 584 << if using auto-tuning\n\nShared Pool Size: 0 0 << ideal to set a minimum\n\nStreams Pool Size: 0 0\n\n15 rows selected.\n\nSetting\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDB Files: 200\n\nOpen Cursors: 300 << larger values require more memory for the Library Cache\n\nProcesses: 150\n\nSession Cached Cursors: 25\n\nSessions: 170\n\nSetting\n\n------------------------------\n\nCache Advice: ON\n\nCompatible: 10.2.0.1.0\n\nCursor Sharing: EXACT\n\nQuery Rewrite: TRUE\n\nStatistics Level: TYPICAL << necessary for internal analysis to auto-tune\n\nResource Current HWM Setting\n\n------------------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------\n\nprocesses 25 26 150\n\nsessions 29 30 170\n\nenqueue_locks 21 28 2300\n\nenqueue_resources 21 21 968\n\nges_procs 0 0 0\n\ndml_locks 0 8 748\n\nmax_shared_servers 2 2 UNLIMITED\n\n14 rows selected.\n\nDouble underscore parameters below are the "current" auto-tuned size of the component.\n\nParameter Session Value Instance Value\n\n----------------------------------- ------------------------- -------------------------\n\n_4031_dump_bitvec 67194879 67194879\n\n_4031_max_dumps 3600 3600\n\n_PX_use_large_pool FALSE FALSE\n\n__db_cache_size 503316480 503316480\n\n_shared_pool_reserved_pct 5 5\n\nevent 10235 trace name context 10235 trace name context\n\nforever, level 65536 forever, level 65536SGAComponents.sql (need to run appropriate code for release level)\n\nREM Important information for investigating the efficiency with auto-tuning\n\nREM Most problems with auto-tuning will show up in sections 3 and 4 of this report\n\nREM\n\nREM In this sample, the last couple of sessions are not listed. These show high and low\n\nREM memory usage over time and a breakdown of SGA information from V$SGAINFO\n\nREM\n\nREM Trends to be watching for:\n\nREM Are there no rows of data showing auto-tuning is making memory changes?\n\nREM Are there periods of time where one component grows and grows and then it shrinks and shrinks\n\nREM as the original component grows and grows? This points to "fighting" for memory\n\nREM Are there repeated rows with STATUS=\'ERROR\'\n\nREM\n\nREM These cases indicate that SGA_TARGET is too small\n\nREM\n\nREM Caveat: Memory moves go through the default Buffer Cache. So a move required in the\n\nREM Streams Pool may take memory from 1) the Shared Pool, and then 2) to the Buffer Cache, and\n\nREM then 3) to the Streams Pool. Therefore, excess memory within SGA_TARGET that is not\n\nREM needed within components in the SGA will collect in the default Buffer Cache. In other words,\n\nREM as the SGA stabilizes, the default Buffer Cache can be oversized.\n\nCOMPONENT Current Size Min Size Max Size Granule Size\n\n----------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------\n\nshared pool 285,212,672 276,824,064 0 8,388,608\n\nlarge pool 8,388,608 8,388,608 0 8,388,608\n\njava pool 8,388,608 8,388,608 0 8,388,608\n\nstreams pool 0 0 0 8,388,608\n\nDEFAULT buffer cache 754,974,720 754,974,720 0 8,388,608\n\nKEEP buffer cache 0 0 0 8,388,608\n\nRECYCLE buffer cache 0 0 0 8,388,608\n\nDEFAULT 2K buffer cache 0 0 0 8,388,608\n\nDEFAULT 4K buffer cache 0 0 0 8,388,608\n\nDEFAULT 8K buffer cache 0 0 0 8,388,608\n\nDEFAULT 16K buffer cache 0 0 0 8,388,608\n\nDEFAULT 32K buffer cache 0 0 0 8,388,608\n\nASM Buffer Cache 0 0 0 8,388,608\n\n----------------\n\nsum 1,056,964,608\n\nCOMPONENT Type Mode Timestamp\n\n------------------------ --------------- --------------- --------------------\n\nshared pool GROW IMMEDIATE 08/12/2007 11:42:32\n\nlarge pool STATIC\n\njava pool STATIC\n\nstreams pool STATIC\n\nDEFAULT buffer cache SHRINK IMMEDIATE 08/12/2007 11:42:32\n\nKEEP buffer cache STATIC\n\nRECYCLE buffer cache STATIC\n\nDEFAULT 2K buffer cache STATIC\n\nDEFAULT 4K buffer cache STATIC\n\nDEFAULT 8K buffer cache STATIC\n\nDEFAULT 16K buffer cache STATIC\n\nDEFAULT 32K buffer cache STATIC\n\nASM Buffer Cache STATIC\n\nCOMPONENT . . . Final Status Changed At\n\n------------------ ----------- -------- -------------------\n\nshared pool 276,824,064 COMPLETE 08/12/2007 11:40:24\n\nlarge pool 8,388,608 COMPLETE 08/12/2007 11:40:24\n\nDEFAULT buffer cache 763,363,328 COMPLETE 08/12/2007 11:40:24\n\njava pool 8,388,608 COMPLETE 08/12/2007 11:40:24\n\nstreams pool 0 COMPLETE 08/12/2007 11:40:24\n\nDEFAULT buffer cache 763,363,328 COMPLETE 08/12/2007 11:40:24\n\nKEEP buffer cache 0 COMPLETE 08/12/2007 11:40:24\n\nRECYCLE buffer cache 0 COMPLETE 08/12/2007 11:40:24\n\n.\n\n.\n\n.\n\nASM Buffer Cache 0 COMPLETE 08/12/2007 11:40:24\n\nDEFAULT buffer cache 754,974,720 COMPLETE 08/12/2007 11:42:32\n\nshared pool 285,212,672 COMPLETE 08/12/2007 11:42:32CursorEfficiency.sql\n\nMax\n\nREM Best used to investigate the efficiency of open_cursors\n\nREM\n\nREM session_cache_cursors can show 100% usage even though the parameter\n\nREM is undersized. This parameter is not necessary in many environments.\n\nREM\n\nREM The goal with open_cursors is to get the usage percentage up close to 100%\n\nInit Parameter Limit Usage\n\n---------------------------------------- ------- ---------\n\nsession_cached_cursors 25 100%\n\nopen_cursors 300 19%SGAStat.sql\n\nExcellent query to gather trend data prior to 10g. For 10g, see Trendsgastats.sql.\n\nREM This data is for a point-in-time. It is necessary to gather this data at intervals to\n\nREM build trend data for where memory is growing and stabilizing\n\nfree memory 23,273,108 sql area 12,810,916 library cache 7,691,788 ASH buffers 4,194,304 KCB Table Scan Buffer 3,981,204 KSFD SGA I/O b 3,977,128 row cache 3,741,868 KQR M SO 3,621,804 CCursor 3,308,648 . . . ---------------- Tot 114,520,848\n\n分析某个特定组件的趋势情况（里面的name 依据AWR shared pool 某个增长最快的组件名称做相应调整，时间调到需要趋势分析的最早时间）：\n\n/* Hisotry K* usage */\n\nset serveroutput on;\n\nexec dbms_output.put_line(\'Hisotry KSXR pending messages que usage\');\n\nselect bytes/1024/1024 , s.snap_id, begin_interval_time START_TIME\n\nfrom dba_hist_sgastat g, dba_hist_snapshot s\n\nwhere name=\'KSXR pending messages que\'\n\nand pool=\'shared pool\'\n\nand trunc(begin_interval_time) >= \'01-DEC-2013\'\n\nand s.snap_id = g.snap_id\n\norder by 2;\n\n/* Shared Pool 某天历史分配情况 */\n\nset serveroutput on;\n\nexec dbms_output.put_line(\'history of Shared pool allocations in a speciifed Day\');\n\ncol name format a30\n\nselect n,\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 1,bytes, null)) "1",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 2,bytes, null)) "2",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 3,bytes, null)) "3",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 4,bytes, null)) "4",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 5,bytes, null)) "5",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 6,bytes, null)) "6",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 7,bytes, null)) "7",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 8,bytes, null)) "8",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 9,bytes, null)) "9",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 10,bytes, null)) "10",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 11,bytes, null)) "11",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 12,bytes, null)) "12",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 13,bytes, null)) "13",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 14,bytes, null)) "14",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 15,bytes, null)) "15",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 16,bytes, null)) "16",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 17,bytes, null)) "17",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 18,bytes, null)) "18",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 19,bytes, null)) "19",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 20,bytes, null)) "20",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 21,bytes, null)) "21",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 22,bytes, null)) "22",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 23,bytes, null)) "23",\n\nmax(decode(to_char(begin_interval_time, \'hh24\'), 24,bytes, null)) "24"\n\nfrom (select \'"\'||name||\'"\' n, begin_interval_time, bytes from dba_hist_sgastat a, dba_hist_snapshot b\n\nwhere pool=\'shared pool\' and a.snap_id=b.snap_id\n\nand to_char(begin_interval_time,\'hh24:mi\') between \'01:00\' and \'24:00\'\n\nand to_char(begin_interval_time,\'dd-mon\') = to_char(sysdate-1, \'dd-mon\'));\n\n对于4031 的深入以及代码层面分析，Oracle 后台研发一般需要 heapdump 或者 library cache dump 进行分析.\n\n1) Heapdump 的信息: 命令如下：\n\nsqlplus /nolog\n\nconnect / as sysdba\n\noradebug setmypid\n\noradebug unlimit\n\noradebug dump heapdump 536871426\n\noradebug tracefile_name\n\noradebug close_trace\n\n影响分析：\n\n从经验来看，一般Heapdump 执行不会对系统造成太多的影响，影响基本可以忽略。\n\n如果产生影响，也是系统产生4031后影响结果，非本身该操作影响。\n\n2) 根据需要可以做library cache dump. 命令 如下：\n\nSQL> ALTER SYSTEM SET EVENTS \'IMMEDIATE TRACE NAME LIBRARY_CACHE LEVEL 16\';\n\n影响分析：\n\n从经验来看，library cache dump可能会对系统有些少许的影响(依据系统负载不同而影响不同)，建议可以在晚上非业务高峰期做。\n\n执行Heapdump以及librarcy cache dump 有必要时可以联系 oracle 支持进行指导.\n\n## Listener问题\n\n如出现Listner 连接不上或者慢这样的问题，一般的需要信息搜集下：\n\n* 基本描述：远程连接慢不慢，本地连接慢不慢，加不加TNS有没有影响，sys用户连接有没有影响.\n* sqlnet.ora和listene.ora信息\n* AWR/ASH 报告 参考日常运维-工具介绍章节ASH和AWR\n* 用户执行的命令和错误输出.\n* 数据库发生故障时的近几个小时的连接情况等. 如 DBA_HIST_RESOURCE_LIMIT等.\n* 检查是否可以在数据库本机通过：sqlplus / as sysdba 登录数据库\n* 在实际操作中，客户会使用如下方法进行实际信息的搜集。\n\nAIX： truss –Dlafeo /tmp/truss-lsnr.log -p <PID_of_listener>\n\n* 官方文档的列到的可以参考的命令如下.\n\nO/S Trace Utility\n\n----------- ------------------------------------------------------\n\nSun Solaris truss, e.g.: $ truss –efldDE -o <output file> -p <executable>\n\nHP/UX tusc, eg : $ tusc -afpo <output file> -T "%H:%M:%S" -p <executable>\n\nIBM AIX truss, e.g.: $ truss -Dlaefo <output file> -p <executable>\n\nLinux strace, eg : $ strace -fo <output file> <executable>\n\n-- 等2分钟然后停止这个truss/strace/tusc进程\n\n因为不同平台的具体版本可能稍有不同，如有些参数有些变化，请以OS 信息为准.\n\n* 如果需要Listner 更细的诊断信息，需要打开SQL-NET Trace跟踪. 因此为高阶内容，不在此详细列出，可以参考文档1681696.1.\n\n## 强制SQL重新解析\n\n以下步骤将强制SQL重新解析：\n\n1. 确认问题SQL的SQL_ID（通过OEM、后台SQL查询、AWR）和当前执行计划：\n\nSQL> set line 200 pagesize 1000\n\nSQL> set long 99999999\n\nSQL> col SQL_ID for a15\n\nSQL> select INST_ID, SQL_ID, SQL_FULLTEXT\n\nfrom gv$sql\n\nwhere SQL_FULLTEXT like \'select%\'\n\norder by 1 desc, 2;\n\n【注意】\n\n* 其中where条件中select为关键字，可多个关键字组合查询（例如\'select%odt0101%\'），关键字中间用%连接，必须完全匹配大小写。\n* 从共享池中已经被刷出去的SQL无法从这个视图中查询出来\n\n1. 根据SQL_ID查询问题SQL对应hash地址等参数\n\nSQL> select SQL_ID, SQL_TEXT, ADDRESS, HASH_VALUE\n\nfrom v$sqlarea\n\nwhere SQL_ID = \'xxxxx\';\n\n【注意】\n\n* xxxxx为第1步中查出的SQL_ID，需要自行更改并带入语句中\n* 需要到对应运行节点进行查询\n\n1. 确认该SQL目前在数据库中未执行（针对RAC环境）\n\nSQL> select * from gv$session where sql_id = \'xxxxx\';\n\n【注意】\n\n* 无返回值代表此语句未在执行中\n\n1. 手工方式kill 掉SQL #针对正在执行中情况，需要联系业务人员确认\n\nSQL> alter system kill session \'sid ,serial#\';\n\n【注意】\n\n* sid, serial#需替换为第3步中查到的对应值\n\n1. 清理该SQL的内存中的SQL执行计划（针对RAC环境）\n\nSQL> exec dbms_shared_pool.purge(\'ADDRESS,HASH_VALUE\',\'C\');\n\n【注意】\n\n* ADDRESS,HASH_VALUE需替换为第2步中查到的对应值\n* 需要到对应运行节点执行\n\nOracle Corporation is the world\'s largest enterprise software company. With annual revenues of more than $10.8 billion, Oracle offers its database, tools and application products, along with related consulting, education, and support services.\n\nOracle Support Services provides technical and operational expertise for all Oracle technology and applications.\n\nOracle is a registered trademark of Oracle Corporation. Other names may be trademarks of their respective owners.\n\nAll Rights Reserved. No part of this publication may be reprinted or otherwise reproduced without permission from the publisher.\n\nCopyright © 2012 Oracle Corporation.\n\n', 'score': 0.3690219521522522}]
